{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1473093-supernatural-concealment-traits","id":1473093,"title":"Supernatural concealment traits.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-01-23T12:03:07-08:00","id":1473093,"title":"Supernatural concealment traits.","content":"Why do Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, Mummy, Promethean, and Changeling have defined terms such as Masquerade, Lunacy, Quiesence, Sybaris, Disquiet, and the Mask respectively that either conceal the protagonists supernatural status from mundane humanity or negatively impact them in some way, but to my knowledge Hunter, Geist, Demon, Beast, and Deviant do not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24961-darklander","name":"Darklander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-23T12:22:46-08:00","id":1473095,"title":"","content":"You've brought up a number of different things with wildly different meanings. Here's a few examples of how they are so different to each other:<br /> The Masquerade is wholly a social construct that protects vampires. It's a tradition that serves a practical reason.<br /> Quiescence is a magical phenomenon that is to the detriment of mages and in fact <i>protects</i> normal humans rather than the other way around. Without it, mages would almost certainly be the rulers of this world.<br /> The Mask covers things that could not be explained away in any form. It covers aspects that can't otherwise be hidden in any real way and is key for changelings to actually function at all ironside.<br /> Disquiet is what you get when a Promethean <i>fails</i> to keep themselves hidden. It attracts negative attention so it's actually the completely opposite of all the aforementioned terms.<br /> <br /> Hunters are mostly just mundane humans.<br /> Demons have Covers that hide them both from humans and the God-Machine.<br /> Deviants hide from regular people just like vampires, but simply have no specific term for it since deviants don't form societies the same way that vampires do and thus has less common vernacular. Also, having a supernatural curtain to hide behind would remove a huge chunk of the game's appeal.<br /> <br /> You wonder why some splats have a system for supernatural concealment against humans while others don't, but phrasing it that way just hides how different all those systems really are and what purposes they serve in those specific games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-23T13:23:28-08:00","id":1473103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darklander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1473093-supernatural-concealment-traits#post1473093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, Mummy, Promethean, and Changeling have defined terms such as Masquerade, Lunacy, Quiesence, Sybaris, Disquiet, and the Mask respectively that either conceal the protagonists supernatural status from mundane humanity or negatively impact them in some way, but to my knowledge Hunter, Geist, Demon, Beast, and Deviant do not?</div> </div> </div> </div>To add onto Tessie's observation above:<br /> <br /> Three of the five games without a specifically-named magical widget (or two-and-a-half, depending) are built with characters working primarily with, against, and/or amidst explicitly conspiratorial groups who can supplement humanity's inclination to look the other way with temporal and magical coverup methods.<br /> <br /> The remaining two concern characters that work with traumatic actions and the byproducts thereof and have operated without entrenched global culture for most of human history, and the other half of Hunter likewise factors into this group due to the way the Code works with relation to normal breaking points around the supernatural.<br /> <br /> They don't have a generalized mystic-psychic phenomenon directly working on witnesses' minds and they're close enough to mundane humanity to recognize that most people just aren't wired to want to talk about the sort of things they deal with on a regular basis. That's pretty much it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}